# Docker ignore file for the repository-root build context
# (seller-server/Dockerfile is built with `context: .`).
#
# Everything here is either rebuilt output, VCS metadata, or docs — none of it
# is needed to compile the crate, and `target/` in particular is hundreds of
# megabytes of host (glibc 2.39) artefacts that must never be shipped in the
# build context.
#
# Note: seller-server/.dockerignore is now inert — Docker only reads a
# .dockerignore sitting at the root of the context in use.

# Build output
target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# VCS + CI metadata
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/

# Node / Anchor tooling
node_modules/
.anchor/
.yarn/
test-ledger/

# Documentation
*.md

# Local environment (keep .env.example — the runtime stage copies it in)
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# IDE / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
